    description: "Discovered during INV-jofaf facet 2 cleanup (2026-04-11). Two scenarios in `.githooks/test_hooks.sh` have been silently failing without anyone noticing:\n\n## Failing scenarios\n\n### Scenario 8c: \"No state file → full reflection checklist\"\nExpected output: `decision=block` with `Stale reflection` in the REASON string.\nActual output: `{\"decision\": \"approve\", \"reason\": \"Interactive session (PID does not match autonomous agent)\"}`\n\nThe hook is short-circuiting on the PID ancestor walk — it sees the stored autonomous PID in AUTONOMOUS_MODE.txt but cannot walk the current process ancestor chain to verify it matches, so it classifies the test sandbox invocation as \"interactive\" and approves the stop. The test then asserts \"block\" and \"Stale reflection\" and fails.\n\n### Scenario 8d-1: \"Dead PID re-claim (crash recovery)\"\nExpected: dead PID in AUTONOMOUS_MODE.txt (999999999) is re-claimed by the hook, stop is blocked, AUTONOMOUS_MODE.txt is updated with a new PID.\nActual: `{\"decision\": \"approve\", \"reason\": \"Interactive session (PID does not match autonomous agent)\"}` — same short-circuit.\n\nThe hook was supposed to detect that PID 999999999 is not an ancestor of the test process AND not currently running, then RE-CLAIM autonomous ownership with the test's own PID. Instead it approves as \"interactive\".\n\n## Evidence that these are pre-existing\n\nI verified by running `git stash && bash .githooks/test_hooks.sh` against the pre-my-changes state (before INV-jofaf facet 2 started modifying stop_logic.sh). Both scenarios failed with IDENTICAL output. So these failures pre-date every recent change — they have been failing for an unknown duration, invisibly, because nothing in CI runs test_hooks.sh (verified by grepping the CI workflow files for the script name).\n\n## Root-cause hypothesis\n\nThe PID ancestor walk in stop.sh calls `_is_pid_ancestor` which walks `/proc/$PID/ppid` up the chain. In the test sandbox:\n1. Test spawns `bash run_stop_hook.sh <sandbox_repo>` as a subprocess\n2. run_stop_hook.sh exec's the real stop.sh\n3. stop.sh sources stop_logic.sh\n4. stop_logic.sh reads AUTONOMOUS_MODE.txt (in sandbox) — has stored PID\n5. stop_logic.sh walks CURRENT process ancestor chain looking for that PID\n6. Current process is stop.sh → run_stop_hook.sh → bash → test_hooks.sh → bash (the test shell). None of those PIDs match the stored autonomous PID.\n7. SESSION_IS_AUTONOMOUS becomes false\n8. Hook approves as \"interactive\"\n\nThe test scenario intent was probably: \"if there's no state file (8c) or a dead PID (8d-1), re-claim autonomy and proceed to Path 1/2/3\". The current code short-circuits BEFORE that re-claim happens, because the PID mismatch check runs first and wins.\n\nWhether the original intent is still correct is itself an open question — maybe the PID guard IS what we want, and scenarios 8c/8d-1 are testing a stale contract that no longer holds.\n\n## Impact\n\nLow — the scenarios are specific test cases that test edge cases of PID re-claim / state-file bootstrapping. The main stop hook flow (scenarios 8a via INV-jofaf's fix, 8b, 8d-2) is tested and works. But the failure is invisible because:\n1. test_hooks.sh is not in CI (confirmed — not run by any workflow file)\n2. The pre-push hook is the only time it runs manually, and most agents probably don't run it regularly\n3. Nobody noticed the failures because the test output scrolls by during manual runs and the \"SUMMARY: X passed, Y failed\" line is easy to miss\n\n## Fix options\n\n1. **Fix the scenarios**: update test sandbox to use a stored PID that matches the current process's ancestor chain (e.g., use `$BASHPID` or walk down to ensure the test-owned PID is stored). Make the test's fake autonomous session appear as a real ancestor.\n2. **Fix the hook**: if the scenarios represent valid use cases (dead PID, missing state), the hook should handle them correctly even from a non-ancestor process context.\n3. **Delete the scenarios**: if the tested behavior is no longer desired, remove the tests entirely rather than leaving them as silent failures.\n4. **Put test_hooks.sh in CI**: add a workflow job that runs `bash .githooks/test_hooks.sh` so silent failures become loud. This should happen REGARDLESS of which fix option is chosen.\n\n## Prior context\n\nCommit `c87fdf577` (\"fix(hooks): fix circuit breaker TOCTOU race and off-by-one in stop hook\") modified stop hook logic around the time this might have been introduced. `df28b4698` (\"fix: throttle stop hook hash recording to prevent premature circuit breaker trips\") is another recent stop hook change. Neither commit explicitly addresses test_hooks.sh.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nFix option 4 (add test_hooks.sh to CI) immediately — it takes ~10 seconds to run and would have caught this on the first broken commit. Then investigate options 1-3 with the benefit of CI feedback.\n\nSeparate from fixing: audit the repo for other scripts/tests that live under `.githooks/` or `scripts/` and check whether any are reachable from CI. Likely candidates for \"silently broken for months\" status.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis item is about a LATENT TEST REGRESSION and its ROOT INFRASTRUCTURE GAP (no CI for bash tests). Not about INV-jofaf facet 2, which just happened to be the work that surfaced it.\n\nRelated: lab notebook entry `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_04102026_2100.md` captures the broader session findings."  # 39a6
    fields:  # 39a6
      statement: "Every bash test in .githooks/test_hooks.sh must be either passing or loudly failing. Silent test failures must not be possible — if a test regresses, CI must fail."  # 39a6
      root_cause: ".githooks/test_hooks.sh is a bash test script that is not invoked by any CI workflow. Scenarios 8c and 8d-1 have been failing for an unknown duration without surfacing, because the pre-push hook is the only time the script runs manually and the SUMMARY line is easy to miss. The failing assertions are on PID ancestor walk behavior in stop_logic.sh: the scenarios expect a 'dead PID re-claim / missing state file → re-claim + block' flow, but the hook short-circuits on 'Interactive session (PID does not match autonomous agent)' before reaching that path."  # 39a6
